findings.comment:
750.800e - The following non-food contact surfaces were soiled:
A) storage cabinets buffet units out front (splash and crumbs);
B) under coffee maker and behind soda machines (dust/debris);
C) top of soft serve machine (splash);
D) under/around microwave on fry line (food splash/buildup);
E) reach-in freezer on fry line - gaskets (general buildup);
F) bottom inside warmer (food debris);   and
G) onion and potato storage in back prep (general buildup).

Clean non-food contact surfaces daily/as needed to eliminate buildup of debris.

750.800b - The following food contact surfaces were soiled:
A) top of magnetic knife strip in dish area (dust/debris);
B) can opener blade & holder (buildup);
C) white baffle inside ice machine (mold);
D) fan on table blowing in prep area (dust);  and
E) ice shoots on soda machines (mold).

Clean and sanitize food contact surfaces between uses/as needed to prevent cross contamination and eliminate buildup of debris. In-use equipment (i.e. can opener, slicers, cutting boards, etc.) must go through ware washing up to every 4hrs after continuous use.

750.800e - The following non-food contact surfaces were soiled:
A) under microwave in back prep (shelf with crumbs/dust);
B) fryers (grease on sides);
C) bottom inside dough cooler (crumbs);
D) bottom ledge inside both small prep coolers (food debris under condenser);
E) floor fan (dust);
F) inside cabinets at drink counter (moisture/splash);
G) under/behind soda machines at drink counter (dust/debris);
H) inside cabinets at dessert bar (debris)
I) under ice cream machine (dust);  
J) lower shelves of prep tables (food/general debris);  and
K) wire shelving - especially lower shelves and wheels (buildup).

Clean non-food contact surfaces daily/as needed to eliminate buildup of debris.

750.800e - The following non-food contact surfaces were soiled:
A) dish machine - general surfaces on outside/junctures (splash/buildup);
B) under BUNN hot water dispenser (debris);
C) #10 can rack (splash/food debris);
D) under coffee maker and soda machine next to coffee maker at the drink counter (beans/dust);   and
E) sides of fryers (grease/food debris).

Clean non-food contact surfaces daily/as needed to eliminate buildup of debris.

findings.citation_text:
750.1220 - Floors were soiled in the following areas:
A) walkin freezer (ice/general debris);
B) under/behind fryers (grease/food debris);   
C) along wall under dish machine (food/debris);  and
D) under ice machine (disposable drinking cups/debris).

Clean floors as needed under equipment to eliminate buildup of debris.

